209-### 2.5 State directory and trust record location
210-
211-- `stateDir(dir)`: run `git rev-parse --path-format=absolute
212-  --git-common-dir` with working directory `dir`; trim the output; result
213-  is `<output>/roast`. If git fails (not a repository), the error message
214-  is `not inside a git repository`.
215-- `trustPath(dir)` is `<stateDir(dir)>/trust.json`; on failure the error is
216-  `trust: not inside a git repository`.
217-- Linked worktrees resolve to the main repository's common dir, so they
218-  share one record.
219-- Every trust operation from the CLI passes the Git toplevel of the
220-  process working directory (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`), not the
221-  directory of a `--config` file.
222-
223-### 2.6 Trust record file (`trust.json`)
224-
225-Version 2 shape, written by the TypeScript implementation:
226-
227-```json
228-{
229-  "version": 2,
230-  "approved": [
231:    "sha256:2b18773b1f654fbbd02019247674005c4035f3972cfc8552655a09bb2ac57d27"
232-  ]
233-}
234-```
235-
236-- Serialized with 2-space indentation, member order `version`, `approved`,
237-  and a trailing newline (`JSON.stringify(rec, null, 2) + "\n"`).
238-- `approved` lists hashes in the order they were approved; no duplicates.
239-- There is no `untrust` command. Deleting the file withdraws every approval
240-  for the clone.
241-
242-**Reading** (`readTrustRecord(path)`) yields one of:
243-
244-| file state | result |
245-|---|---|
246-| absent (`ENOENT`) | `{kind:'current', approved:[]}` |
247-| JSON object, `version` is the number `2` | `{kind:'current', approved}` |
248-| JSON object, `version` is the number `1` | `{kind:'legacy'}` |
249-| anything else | error |
250-
251-- For version 2: `approved` missing or `null` reads as `[]`; otherwise it
252-  must be an array of strings, else error. Unknown top-level members are
253-  ignored on read (Go parity) and dropped on the next write.
254-- For version 1 (written by the Go implementation): nothing else in the
255-  file is read or validated. Its hashes are never compared: the Go hash
256-  serialization is not reproduced (ADR-0003).
257-- Errors: unreadable file -> `read trust record: <cause>`; invalid JSON or
258-  a non-object or wrongly typed `approved` -> `read trust record <path>:
259-  <cause>`; `version` missing or any value other than 1 or 2 -> `trust
260-  record <path> has unsupported version <v>`. Errors are never treated as
261-  "not approved"; they propagate (2.8).
262-
263-**Approved check** (`isApproved(dir, hash)`) returns `'approved'`,
264-`'not-approved'`, or `'legacy'` (record is version 1), or throws.
265-
266-**Approving** (`approve(dir, hash)`):
--
