542:### 2.14 Doctor (reference only; doctor area owns it)
543-
544-- `config-trust` check: pass `no approval required ...` when
545-  `!requiresApproval`; fail when outside a Git repository, when the record
546-  cannot be read (`approval required; could not read approvals: <err>`),
547-  or when not approved (`... endpoint probes skipped; run `npx roast
548-  trust``); pass when approved. In TS, a `'legacy'` (version 1) record is a
549-  fail whose detail says `approved by an older Roast` and names
550-  `npx roast trust`. Doctor never prompts and never approves.
551:- When not trusted, doctor skips the endpoint and round-trip probes for
552-  every role (the probes would send credentials to an unapproved
553-  destination).
554-- `project-credentials` / `user-credentials` checks: for each scope whose
555-  path resolves and whose file exists (`lstat`), `loadCredentials`; fail
556-  with the load error, else pass with `<path> (<sorted providers>)` or
557:  `<path> (none stored)`. A broken file fails doctor even when environment
558-  credentials shadow it.
